1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:01,500
Morning!

2
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:03,450
Best coffee on the island!

3
00:00:05,077 --> 00:00:07,907
Today, you can see a number over everyone's head.

4
00:00:07,957 --> 00:00:10,575
It counts every lie they've told today.

5
00:00:10,625 --> 00:00:11,935
Mo's coffee is fine.

6
00:00:11,985 --> 00:00:13,245
It is not the best.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,870
Most of the numbers are tiny.

8
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:17,260
And then there's Pip.

9
00:00:17,424 --> 00:00:19,214
Good morning, gorgeous!

10
00:00:19,264 --> 00:00:20,604
Love the shoes!

11
00:00:21,411 --> 00:00:22,241
37.

12
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:24,351
It's 731 in the morning.

13
00:00:24,563 --> 00:00:26,113
By midnight, you'll know why.

14
00:00:26,163 --> 00:00:27,903
And you won't like your own number.

15
00:00:31,099 --> 00:00:31,849
Rule one.

16
00:00:31,899 --> 00:00:34,199
It counts every lie, big or small.

17
00:00:34,422 --> 00:00:35,092
Rule two.

18
00:00:35,142 --> 00:00:36,722
It resets at midnight.

19
00:00:36,849 --> 00:00:37,679
Rule three.

20
00:00:37,729 --> 00:00:39,229
Nobody else can see it.

21
00:00:40,446 --> 00:00:41,916
You check the whole island.

22
00:00:41,966 --> 00:00:42,476
Zero.

23
00:00:42,526 --> 00:00:43,036
Zero.

24
00:00:43,086 --> 00:00:44,086
Zero.

25
00:00:44,667 --> 00:00:50,137
In one survey of a thousand American adults, about six in ten said they hadn't told a

26
00:00:50,187 --> 00:00:51,527
single lie that day.

27
00:00:52,702 --> 00:00:54,362
So who is Pip lying to?

28
00:00:56,115 --> 00:00:57,025
Bea!

29
00:00:57,075 --> 00:00:58,865
Your new haircut?

30
00:00:58,915 --> 00:01:00,495
Stunning!

31
00:01:02,643 --> 00:01:06,703
Finn Big- Biggest fish I've ever seen.

32
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:09,200
Nope!

33
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:10,830
Nowhere near the bakery!

34
00:01:12,023 --> 00:01:17,123
In that same survey, half of all the lies came from about five people in every hundred.

35
00:01:17,372 --> 00:01:19,482
A few people tell most of the lies.

36
00:01:19,532 --> 00:01:21,752
And today, one of them is Pip.

37
00:01:23,748 --> 00:01:24,418
Saturday?

38
00:01:24,468 --> 00:01:25,778
No, nothing planned!

39
00:01:25,828 --> 00:01:26,828
Why?

40
00:01:29,064 --> 00:01:30,054
Busy me?

41
00:01:30,104 --> 00:01:32,244
No, I'm I'm just shopping.

42
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:36,700
By the afternoon, everyone you love is lying to you.

43
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:38,970
And without this power, you'd never know.

44
00:01:39,414 --> 00:01:45,314
People catch a lie only about 54% of the time, barely better than flipping a coin.

45
00:01:50,409 --> 00:01:52,949
Okay… can you just come inside?

46
00:01:55,666 --> 00:01:56,766
Surprise!

47
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:01,290
Every lie today was hiding the same thing.

48
00:02:01,539 --> 00:02:07,199
In one diary study, about one in four everyday lies was told for someone else's sake.

49
00:02:08,262 --> 00:02:10,802
I'm a terrible liar.

50
00:02:11,455 --> 00:02:13,835
Even honest people have bad lie days.

51
00:02:18,295 --> 00:02:20,325
And there, in the window, is your own number.

52
00:02:20,375 --> 00:02:21,375
Twelve.

53
00:02:21,611 --> 00:02:22,201
Best ever.

54
00:02:22,251 --> 00:02:22,841
On my way.

55
00:02:22,891 --> 00:02:23,991
I'm not mad.

56
00:02:25,251 --> 00:02:29,601
People in that study said they didn't think their lies were serious, and barely worried

57
00:02:29,651 --> 00:02:30,831
about getting caught.

58
00:02:31,106 --> 00:02:36,736
Researchers who reviewed decades of lie studies suggest we judge other people's lies more

59
00:02:36,786 --> 00:02:38,206
harshly than our own.

60
00:02:42,554 --> 00:02:44,264
You'll never see anyone's number.

61
00:02:44,314 --> 00:02:49,544
But in a study that followed people's lies for three months, almost nine in ten lies were

62
00:02:49,594 --> 00:02:55,224
little white lies, and people said lies were only about 7% of everything they said.

63
00:02:55,274 --> 00:02:58,024
So believing people is usually a safe bet.

64
00:02:58,074 --> 00:03:01,734
And the next time you're about to tell a little one, just notice it.

65
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:04,130
Morning!

66
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:06,240
Pretty good coffee on the island!

67
00:03:08,074 --> 00:03:09,544
Everyone tells a few.

68
00:03:09,594 --> 00:03:12,314
Most people, most of the time, are telling you the truth.
